      "release": {
        "tag_name": "26.09.4",
        "name": "26.09.4",
        "published_at": "2026-11-04T14:20:13Z",
        "html_url": "https://github.com/ankitects/anki/releases/tag/26.09.4",
        "body": "## What's Changed\r\n\r\n**⚠️ This update contains important security fixes. Please upgrade as soon as possible**.\r\n\r\n- Shared decks could execute arbitrary code via iframes when viewed in the editor ([GHSA-j9v5-m549-cg6c](https://github.com/ankitects/anki/security/advisories/GHSA-j9v5-m549-cg6c)). Thanks to @DePierre for the report.\r\n- On macOS, shared decks could execute arbitrary commands via specially crafted image filenames when the \"Show in Folder\" editor action is used ([GHSA-gfvm-4968-jp9m](https://github.com/ankitects/anki/security/advisories/GHSA-gfvm-4968-jp9m)). Thanks to @hyperreality and @Hama1cco for the reports.\r\n- Compromised eMudhra intermediate CA certificates are now disallowed. This is in response to a [widespread security incident](https://emudhra.we-have-a-problem.com/) affecting most systems and web browsers. **Updating Anki might not be enough. Please make sure your system is fully up to date.**\r\n\r\n**Full Changelog**: https://github.com/ankitects/anki/compare/26.09.3...26.09.4",
